            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FAW03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Fawcett</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1769-08-29">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1837"/>
                    <occupation>actor</occupation>
                    <occupation>playwright</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Fawcett was a low comedian who made his London debut at Covent Garden in 1791. George Colman made him stage-manager of at the Haymarket in 
  1799. Colman then wrote a series of plays with Fawcett in mind which confirmed the actor's reputation. </p>
                        <p>The attribution is made on the basis that the encounter, a meal at <persName key="COO01">Thomas Abthorpe Cooper's</persName> with 
    <persName key="INC02">Charles Incledon</persName> also in attendance, has a theatrical bent.
  Incledon and Fawcett were both involved in a dispute with the proprietors of Covent Garden in 1800. Two later entries to Jo Fawcet have also been coded (1811 and 1821). </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"/>
                    <bibl type="other">See <title>DNB</title></bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
